flowchart TD
    G[Common deterministic record tree] --> S[HyMeKo / XML / YAML / JSON]
    S --> V[Decode all records and assert exact equality]
    V --> F[Hashed fixtures and manifest]
    F --> P[Fresh sequential processes: serialize / AST or DOM / owned records]
    P --> R[Two rounds with Criterion samples and peak memory]
    R --> C[Interactive comparison, exportable plot and bounded conclusions]

%% 2026-09-08 continuation: native AST CPU profile -> one hotspot -> parity tests -> fixed-affinity A/B

    P --> L[Profile: long string scanning]
    L --> W[Safe word-at-a-time delimiter scan]
    W --> T[Scalar oracle, escape and span parity]
    T --> R
    R --> A[Profile AST list growth: singleton seed then immediate resize]
    A --> B[Allocate first pair together; preserve empty and singleton bodies]
    B --> J[Paired baseline / candidate / JSON; correctness and memory gates]
    J --> K{JSON comparison supports parser milestone?}
    K -->|yes| U[Resume original CUDA plan]
    K -->|no| N[Record remaining parser gap and next measured target]
    N --> H[Profile linked and Unicode: reductions, allocation, escapes]
    H --> J
    N --> O[Owned records: parse / borrowed projection / AST destruction]
    O --> M[Consume AST and transfer owned strings; verify exact output]
    M --> J
    J --> Q[Automated same-host baseline gate: pass / regression / inconclusive]
    Q --> V2[Generated gate laws and ownership regressions; 10k / 50k scaling]

    V2 --> F2[PERF-2: fuse AST constructor reductions]
    F2 --> G2[Exact AST/errors; same-host AST and owned-record A/B; rollback gate]

    G2 --> B2[Single grammar plus typed OutputBuilder]
    B2 --> A2[Default native AST: compatibility oracle]
    B2 --> D2[Direct owned records: deferred semantic errors]
    A2 --> X2[Parity, ownership, AST and record performance gates]
    D2 --> X2
